#: Game.Levels.UOV.L07_Capstone
msgid "## Capstone: Full UOV Correctness\n"
"\n"
"We now combine all the pieces to prove the **UOV correctness theorem**:\n"
"\n"
"**If** sigma = S^{-1}(w) and F(w) = y,\n"
"**then** P(sigma) = y.\n"
"\n"
"Proof:\n"
"1. P(sigma) = (F composed with S)(sigma) = F(S(sigma))\n"
"   (definition of composition).\n"
"2. S(sigma) = S(S^{-1}(w)) = w (inverse property).\n"
"3. F(w) = y (given).\n"
"4. Therefore P(sigma) = y.\n"
"\n"
"### Your Task\n"
"\n"
"Given:\n"
"- §0 (the secret linear map S, as a linear equivalence)\n"
"- §1 (the central map F)\n"
"- §2 (the intermediate value (o, v))\n"
"- §3 (the central map gives the target)\n"
"- §4 (the target hash value)\n"
"\n"
"Prove: §5\n"
"\n"
"This is: P(sigma) = y where sigma = S^{-1}(w) and P = F composed with S.\n"
"\n"
"### Strategy\n"
"\n"
"1. Rewrite §6 to §7\n"
"   using §8.\n"
"2. Rewrite §9 to §10 using §11.\n"
"3. The goal becomes §12, which is exactly §13. Use §14."
msgstr ""

